--------------------Sure, based on the given code and the comment provided, we can assert the following:

```cs
public void PUT_InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);

    // @@@ Assert that old count of arrList is equal to or greater than new count after insertion
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Count >= arrList.Count + 1);

    // @@@ Assert that new count of arrList is equal to old count + 1 after insertion
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Count == arrList.Count + 1);

    // @@@ Assert that arrList contains the inserted value x
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Contains(x));

    // @@@ Assert that index of x in arrList is equal to the inserted index
    Debug.Assert(arrList.IndexOf(x) == index);

    // @@@ Assert that last index of x in arrList is greater or equal to the inserted index
    Debug.Assert(arrList.LastIndexOf(x) >= index);

    // @@@ Assert that old count of arrList is equal to or greater than new count after insertion
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Count >= arrList.Count + 1);
}
```

I've made the assumption that arrList.Count + 1 should not be used in multiple places in the code. The correct way to increment the count is by using the Count property after the Insert operation.
